TY  - RPRT
TI  - What is Computational Reproducibility?
AU  - Bleier, Arnim
AB  - Reproducibility is a cornerstone of credible and transparent research in Computational Social Science (CSS) and beyond. This guide offers an introduction to the core concepts, challenges, and practices of computational reproducibility. It outlines a structured framework for understanding reproducibility across three dimensions – form, completeness, and availability of research materials – and offers initial guidance for addressing common barriers related to technical complexity, external dependencies, and human factors. This guide is intended to serve as a starting point for CSS researchers who want to increase the reproducibility of their work and, by doing so, contribute to a culture of openness, accountability, and cumulative scientific progress.
